From 79208d877628bba70b8e53d1eaa1b39cfdd8834d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:16:42 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] logging: structure peer lifecycle and Avalanche finality
 diagnostics

Convert13 Info sites and the matching opt-in Avalanche vote debug site while
preserving levels, all disconnect/timeout/parking/activation branches and exact
readable text. Generic vote IDs carry their vote-item type rather than being
mislabelled block or transaction hashes. Explicitly load the same signed atomic
starting height. Preserve the existing fLogIPs-controlled suffix and expose Addr
only under that same guard; logips=0 stores empty strings, not a remote address.
The real two-node fixture checks both privacy modes, peer metadata, clean stops
and unchanged genesis. Rare timeout/parking/vote failures are not newly forced.
The nullable best-known-block message remains deferred; do not invent a zero
hash for <none>. Native/runtime validation is pending.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0;14 reviewed sites):
